---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';

const path = "/compare/omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms";
const title = "Omnisend after Yotpo Email & SMS: Shopify decisions";
const desc = "Evaluate Omnisend for capture and recovery after Yotpo messaging retirement. The buying decision is whether current channel identities, Shopify events and retained review or loyalty jobs can form a dependable receiving workflow.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is this a choice between two active messaging products?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo messaging is retired. Evaluate Omnisend as a receiving sender and Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty as separate continuing services."
  },
  {
    "question": "Why evaluate Omnisend?",
    "answer": "Its current product catalog offers signup forms, ecommerce automation, email, SMS and web push. Demonstrate the capture sources, recovery exits and eligible channels you require rather than assuming presets establish launch speed."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does email signup authorize SMS or push?",
    "answer": "No. Treat email, phone and browser subscription as separate channel records. Test the actual account and browser permission state, including revocation; an email address does not establish another channel\u2019s eligibility."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can Reviews and Loyalty stay with Yotpo?",
    "answer": "Evaluate them independently. Assign their requests and reward notifications one owner, and prove the connector fields and timing needed by Omnisend. A retained module does not revive Yotpo messaging."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will an automated migration recover everything?",
    "answer": "Do not assume that. Start from files actually held and support-confirmed access, reconcile channel statuses and suppressions, and rebuild entry and exit rules. Historical instructions do not establish current dashboard access."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a 12,000-contact quote include?",
    "answer": "Match send volume, SMS destinations and segments, peak months, retained modules, implementation, staff QA and renewal terms across twelve months. Include a sensitivity up to 18,000 contacts without inventing a savings percentage."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should stop recovery?",
    "answer": "A qualifying purchase, closed preorder, exhausted stock or withdrawn permission should remove obsolete marketing work under the documented rules. Test the recipient and product state at dispatch as well as on entry."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are these measured merchant outcomes?",
    "answer": "No. The merchant baselines and acceptance exercises are proposed inputs. Record your own pass/fail evidence, operator time and uncertain incremental contribution before choosing a plan."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
    <nav><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="catalog-kicker">Migration and buying decision</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Evaluate Omnisend for capture and recovery after Yotpo messaging retirement. The buying decision is whether current channel identities, Shopify events and retained review or loyalty jobs can form a dependable receiving workflow.</p></header>
    <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl"><TldrBox picks={[{"label": "Capture and recovery", "tool": "Omnisend candidate", "reason": "Demonstrate form-source routing and current purchase exits."}, {"label": "Continuing modules", "tool": "Yotpo Reviews/Loyalty", "reason": "Keep useful jobs with explicit sender and event ownership."}, {"label": "Channel expansion", "tool": "Separate eligibility", "reason": "Phone or email identity alone does not authorize every channel."}]} /></div>
    <div class="mt-12 card overflow-x-auto"><table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Omnisend receiving stack</th><th>Existing Yotpo services</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Messaging status</td><td>Current email/SMS/push catalog; verify account scope</td><td>Email/SMS retired</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Capture</td><td>Test forms and channel-status mapping</td><td>Saved source records require reconciliation</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Recovery</td><td>Prove cart, purchase and stock exits</td><td>Do not rely on an old messaging queue</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Reviews and points</td><td>Verify required external events</td><td>Continuing products evaluated independently</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Messaging retirement changes the purchase</h2>
      <p>Yotpo announced full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its messaging login now reports that the SMS dashboard and background services are decommissioned. Reviews and Loyalty continue as separate products; keeping them does not retain a messaging sender. See the <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo sunset announcement</a> and <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">decommission notice</a>. This page evaluates a receiving stack, not a new Yotpo messaging purchase.</p>
      <h2>What the receiving stack must prove</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://www.omnisend.com/features/">Omnisend feature catalog</a> lists signup forms, automation and email, SMS and web push. Evaluate those capabilities against your own identity and event path. Yotpo’s migration announcement names Omnisend as a partner; that relationship does not prove complete data recovery, launch time or account-specific compatibility.</p>
      <p>Begin with one staff-controlled profile for each channel combination, plus an existing unsubscribed profile. Capture a form submission, inspect source and permission fields, then place an order on a second device. Record which identity receives the purchase exit and which browser endpoint remains eligible. Avoid merging profiles merely because a device was shared.</p>
      <h2>Capture acceptance: pottery source changes</h2>
      <p>All six merchant examples below are proposed numeric fixtures. For pottery at 480 orders and $31k monthly revenue, separate class waitlists from glaze-kit interest before the holiday starter-set rush. Submit both forms with one address, then change the preference after a kit offer is queued. Accept the design when the recorded intent determines future promotions and the obsolete offer is canceled without blocking the requested class notice.</p>
      <p>Use kiln-care education only for the purchased item with manufacturer-approved instructions. A gift order should not enroll its recipient in buyer marketing. Ask an operator to explain each inclusion from the profile history; a form total alone cannot demonstrate correct routing.</p>
      <h2>Scarce-stock recovery: vinyl and outdoor catalogs</h2>
      <p>For vinyl at 1,800 orders and $72k monthly revenue, plan 200–400-unit pressings around Record Store Day. Let a proposed 300-unit pressing sell out inside a two-hour send window. Verify the queued message and its landing destination do not offer unavailable stock. Place a full-price order during discount recovery and confirm that all obsolete channel steps exit, including a browser notification tied to the same shopper.</p>
      <p>For outdoor gear at 2,400 orders and $112k monthly revenue before Memorial Day, show different hero tents to ultralight and family-camping interests. Change the interest after enqueueing and verify the selected product at dispatch. Test an email-only profile alongside a separately permissioned push profile; record browser support and revocation behavior rather than promising mobile reach. Use approved product guidance without inventing safety advice.</p>
      <h2>Close events and partial fulfillment</h2>
      <p>For keyboards at 940 orders and $58k monthly revenue, use six-week group buys on $180–$420 kits and switch education across five product pages. This is a mixed basket/deposit fixture: $58k divided by 940 is about $61.70 per order, below the kit range. Do not model every order as a full kit. Close a group buy after recovery entry, then replay stale browse activity; accept only if closed stock cannot restart recovery while eligible education remains available.</p>
      <p>For board games at 1,050 orders and $67k monthly revenue before Essen, split an order into shipped and unallocated lines. A purchase exit should stop cart recovery, but it must not imply every item has shipped. Keep operational allocation updates with their owner, and start review or winback timing only under the documented fulfillment rule. Verify that a retained Yotpo Reviews request does not overlap an Omnisend request.</p>
      <h2>Tea replenishment and retained module events</h2>
      <p>For tea at 720 orders and $44k monthly revenue, test 28–35-day blend-specific windows before the Q4 gift-box peak. Add a gift flag, subscription skip and new purchase after queueing. The receiving workflow should preserve the buyer/recipient distinction, cancel stale replenishment and explain why the next eligible reminder differs. Do not use one customer-level reorder date for every blend.</p>
      <p>If Yotpo Loyalty remains, request an actual integration sample for tier, balance and correction events. Identify the authoritative value, event time and retry policy. Test a reward reversal arriving after a points promotion has queued. If the field cannot be delivered reliably, keep that job with a verified owner rather than displaying stale points in a recovery message.</p>
      <h2>Rebuild without inventing missing history</h2>
      <p>Inventory saved files with dates, source store and channel status coverage. Ask support what remains accessible; never assume a retired dashboard export can be regenerated. Preserve unsubscribes and unknown statuses during mapping. Reconcile rejected rows and a sample of individual identities, not just totals.</p>
      <p>Import into a controlled setup with acquisition flows disabled. Existing customers must not become new signups simply because a file was loaded. Rebuild welcome, cart and post-purchase eligibility before styling templates, then test purchases, permission withdrawal and repeated events. Keep operational Shopify notices with their designated sender. Record when an integration needs manual intervention and who owns that work.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-omnisend">reverse-direction migration guide</a> concentrates on file recovery and import enrollment. Use this page to decide whether the resulting capture and channel workflow is worth buying. Neither page supplies evidence that your account has already passed.</p>
      <h2>Annual economics and acceptance decision</h2>
      <p>Use a 12,000-contact base and 18,000-contact sensitivity, matching monthly messages, peak broadcasts, SMS destinations and segment lengths. Include retained Reviews/Loyalty, connector maintenance, domain setup, QA and exit work. Compare current written offers and renewal terms; do not count retired Yotpo messaging as an available renewal price.</p>
      <p>Proposed fixed-goods calculation: $1,000 list-price sales minus $100 discounts minus $400 unchanged goods cost leaves $500 before messaging and labor. A $20 message charge leaves $480. Goods cost remains $400 when price is discounted. To assess a new workflow, compare incremental contribution against a suitable holdout with uncertainty rather than equating attributed recovery revenue with profit.</p>
      <p>Choose Omnisend when its demonstrated source routing, purchase exits and required channel paths meet your acceptance criteria and annual budget. Keeping Yotpo Reviews or Loyalty can be sensible when those jobs remain valuable with verified event ownership. If the required identity joins or preorder states cannot be represented reliably, evaluate another active sender before expanding channels; there is no active Yotpo messaging option to fall back to.</p>
      <p>Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">selection framework</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">pricing worksheet</a> to record acceptance evidence and contract scope.</p>
    </article>
  </div></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Omnisend after Yotpo messaging FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
